  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper provides asymptotic runtime bounds for a quantum least-squares Monte Carlo (LSM) algorithm for optimal stopping (including American option pricing), showing a near-quadratic improvement in the precision parameter ε over classical LSM under smoothness assumptions on continuation values. For generic Markov models, classical runtime scales as ˜O(T m^4 (T+m^2)/ε^2) versus quantum ˜O(T^2 m^4/ε), and for polynomial bases with n-times differentiable continuation values, classical and quantum runtimes scale as ˜O((5T/ε)^{2+6d/n}) and ˜O((5T/ε)^{1+4d/n}), respectively, with further refinements for Brownian and geometric Brownian motion models.",
